> The magic of this dish lies in the cola itself. The carbonation tenderizes the chicken while the sweetness caramelizes into a lacquer-like glaze. Don't substitute diet cola—the real sugar is essential for that glossy finish. The wings are done when the sauce has reduced to a sticky, amber coating.

== Prepare the Wings ==

Rinse @chicken wings{800%g} and pat completely dry with paper towels. Season lightly with @salt{½%tsp} and @white pepper{¼%tsp}. Set aside.

== Sear the Wings ==

Heat @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in a #wok{} or #deep skillet{} over medium-high heat until shimmering.

Add the chicken wings in a single layer, letting them sear without moving for ~{3%minutes} per side until golden brown. The skin will render fat and become crispy. Remove and set aside.

== Make the Glaze ==

Pour off most of the rendered fat, leaving about @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in the wok.

Add @minced garlic{1%tsp} and @minced ginger{1%tsp}; cook for ~{30%seconds} until fragrant.

Pour in @cola{330%ml} (one can). Add @light soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{1%tbsp}, and @rock sugar{30%g}.

Bring to a vigorous boil, then reduce heat to medium-low.

== Braise the Wings ==

Return the seared chicken wings to the wok. Nestle them in the cola liquid.

Cover and simmer for ~{15%minutes}, turning the wings halfway through. The wings should absorb the color and become stained with the glaze.

== Reduce and Finish ==

Uncover the wok and turn the heat to medium-high. The sauce should now be at a lively simmer.

Cook for another ~{8-10%minutes}, turning the wings occasionally, until the sauce reduces to a thick, glossy syrup that coats the back of a spoon.

The wings should be deeply caramelized with a mahogany glaze. If the sauce reduces too quickly before the wings are done, add water 30%ml at a time.

== Serve ==

Transfer to a serving plate. Optionally sprinkle with @sesame seeds{1%tsp} and @sliced scallions{1%stalk} for visual appeal.

Serve immediately while hot and sticky. Best eaten with bare hands—there's no elegant way to eat sticky cola wings!